{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Sirima","html":"<article id='thag2.20'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.20 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.20 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sirimattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sirima </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Pare ca naṁ pasaṁsanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>If others praise one </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>attā ce asamāhito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who has no immersion, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Moghaṁ pare pasaṁsanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they praise in vain, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>attā hi asamāhito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>as one has no immersion. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pare ca naṁ garahanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>If others criticize one </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>attā ce susamāhito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who does have immersion, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Moghaṁ pare garahanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they criticize in vain, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>attā hi susamāhito”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>as one does have immersion. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Sirimā thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>vaggo dutiyo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Cundo ca jotidāso ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>thero heraññakāni ca; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Somamitto sabbamitto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kāḷo tisso ca kimilo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nando ca sirimā ceva, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dasa therā mahiddhikāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
